{"title":"Mock AIME I 2015 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2015_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the AoPS Carnival, there is a \"Weighted Dice\" game show. This game features two identical looking weighted 6 sided dice. For each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/244ad3efc2d8de7bbdef7a3296ae51999db73e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i\\leq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />, Die A has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/613112022291de6a616658804324ae4a216f6500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{i}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"15\" height=\"21\" /> probability of rolling the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, while Die B has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea96092ea89a532c9ced915d51a9367b8d490e59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{7-i}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"21\" /> probability of rolling <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />. During one session, the host randomly chooses a die, rolls it twice, and announces that the sum of the numbers on the two rolls is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the probability that the die chosen was Die A. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is written as a fraction in lowest terms, find the sum of the numerator and denominator.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2015_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability that A lands at 10 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/3/333d52bd045b69adf554aa1b1e23cf9b6c625bfb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{4 \\cdot 6 + 5 \\cdot 5 + 6 \\cdot 4}{441} = \\dfrac{73}{441}.\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"38\" />\nThe probability that B lands at 10 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccef5cc36ebe94a41e5d7541fae26ad0006bc3c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1 \\cdot 3 + 2 \\cdot 2 + 3 \\cdot 1}{441} = \\dfrac{10}{441}.\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"38\" />\nThe probability that A was picked is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b28e4d2b51873c960ab4bae5d0bfb02115410e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{73}{73+10} = \\dfrac{73}{83}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"107\" height=\"39\" />. The sum of numerator and denominator is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b2d0ea12ede92a31e5facccb864b3898487b9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{156}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017164713\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 57/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2224/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16137:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017164713 and revision id 93498. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}